<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>纽约时报 &amp;gt; 美国 &amp;gt; 政治</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/spotlight/on-politics</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 21:01:44 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>缅因州民主党迎来了一位新的工人阶级英雄：特洛伊·杰克逊。他能交付吗？</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/27/us/politics/troy-jackson-maine-senate-democrats.html</link><description>前伐木工特洛伊·杰克逊面临着击倒苏珊·柯林斯的艰巨任务。</description><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 21:01:44 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/27/us/politics/troy-jackson-maine-senate-democrats.html</guid></item><item><title>夏季与伊朗的战争如何影响秋季选举</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/24/us/politics/republicans-trump-iran-war-midterms.html</link><description>特朗普总统和共和党人似乎无法摆脱冲突的政治影响。</description><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:21:53 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/24/us/politics/republicans-trump-iran-war-midterms.html</guid></item><item><title>左翼的下一个重大考验：密歇根州、威斯康星州和明尼苏达州</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/22/us/politics/progressives-michigan-wisconsin-minnesota.html</link><description>进步人士现在正在紫色或浅蓝色州的更不稳定的地形中战斗。</description><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 21:00:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/22/us/politics/progressives-michigan-wisconsin-minnesota.html</guid></item><item><title>涉及马克·兰姆的性丑闻在亚利桑那州共和党众议院初选中会重要吗？</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/20/us/politics/arizona-house-primary-lamb.html</link><description>在该州一个宗教信仰深厚的地区举行的竞选是对特朗普支持力量的考验。</description><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 22:28:12 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/20/us/politics/arizona-house-primary-lamb.html</guid></item><item><title>谁真正拥有 2026 年中期现金优势？</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/17/us/politics/democrats-republicans-midterms-cash.html</link><description>筹款竞赛比看起来更加激烈。</description><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 21:31:37 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/17/us/politics/democrats-republicans-midterms-cash.html</guid></item><item><title>缅因州民主党的冒险政治实验</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/15/us/politics/maine-democrats-senate-adventure.html</link><description>党的领导人正在进行一项政治实验。</description><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 22:10:18 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/15/us/politics/maine-democrats-senate-adventure.html</guid></item><item><title>2026 年不可思议的中期选举指南以及我们如何走到这一步</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/13/us/politics/midterms-elections-trump.html</link><description>自从我们的作家休育儿假以来，美国政治发生了很多变化。</description><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 21:16:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/13/us/politics/midterms-elections-trump.html</guid></item><item><title>普拉特纳的戏剧再次引发民主党人关于双重标准的争论</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/10/us/politics/platner-democrats-women-double-standard.html</link><description>他的候选资格加剧了民主党人在性别问题以及如何赢回工人阶级选民问题上的紧张关系。</description><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 21:47:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/10/us/politics/platner-democrats-women-double-standard.html</guid></item><item><title>格雷厄姆·普拉特纳什么时候会退学？这是游戏的状态。</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/08/us/politics/platner-democrats-maine-state-of-play.html</link><description>以下是我们对民主党试图罢免参议员苏珊·柯林斯的骚动所了解的情况。</description><pubDate>Wed, 08 Jul 2026 22:10:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/08/us/politics/platner-democrats-maine-state-of-play.html</guid></item><item><title>民意调查对参议院之争有何评价</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/06/us/politics/senate-polls-platner.html</link><description>我们的两名政治记者深入研究了本周的调查。</description><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 22:20:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/06/us/politics/senate-polls-platner.html</guid></item></channel></rss>